<!--Render Target Documentation — V1Scope
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.V1Scope-->
<rdoc:V1Scope xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    V1 base types handled by this target
  </is>
  <documentation>
    V1 supports exactly two base types:

    - com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block — ScadBlockProcessor
      Standard SCAD block module.
    - com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set — ScadSetProcessor
      STEPS-based set with view submodules.

    User types that inherit either base type use the same processor.
    ScadSetProcessor is registered first because it is more specific.
    ScadBlockProcessor is the fallback for Block.

    A block whose baseType chain does not include
    com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block is not supported. The compiler emits
    BML_NO_TARGET for that block.

    isSubtypeOf walks the baseType chain in the BOM type registry.

    Later processors (copy of built-in service files, capability implementation
    transpilation) may be added. They are not required for V1 block and set emit.
    The engine allows them to use a different strategy in the same target.

    ScadBlockProcessor emits a leaf, a composite module, or a preset JSON file.
    ScadSetProcessor emits a SCAD file with a STEPS array and four view
    submodules. A composition that carries bml:each, bml:if, or bml:with
    returns files: [] and diagnostic BML_DIRECTIVE_DEFERRED.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:TargetRegistration" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:V1Scope>
